          "title": "Shenyang Mahjong",
          "subtitle": "Card game",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Shenyang Mahjong is a northeast China Mahjong variant associated with Shenyang and Liaoning region play. It keeps the core draw-discard meld structure while applying local table conventions for win validity and scoring emphasis."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Shenyang Mahjong developed as a regional rule profile within broader Chinese Mahjong traditions and spread through local social play."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "4 players seated by wind position."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard Mahjong set with suited tiles, honor tiles, and bonus tiles according to table profile."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard Mahjong set with suited tiles, honor tiles, and bonus tiles according to table profile."
            },
